config.objective:
Experimental agent steps must be enabled and an authenticated Codex or Claude Code account must be selected; abort and state that exact requirement if the agent cannot run. Investigate this Rust repository using the bug report and reproduction expectations below. Identify the owning module, inspect relevant implementation and existing tests, and add the smallest focused regression test that reproduces the bug. Run that focused test and confirm it fails for the expected reason. Do not edit production code, do not fix the bug, and do not make unrelated changes. Bug report: ${input.bug_report}
Reproduction expectations: ${input.reproduction_expectations}
Return only one JSON object with exactly these keys: diagnosis (concise evidence-based root-cause diagnosis), cargo_args (JSON array of arguments following the cargo executable that deterministically reruns only the focused regression), failing_test_evidence (concise command and observed expected failure), and regression_test_path (repository-relative path).

config.inline:
const fs = require('fs');
const cp = require('child_process');
const cargoArgs = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8'));
if (!Array.isArray(cargoArgs) || cargoArgs.some(x => typeof x !== 'string')) throw new Error('cargo_args must be an array of strings');
const r = cp.spawnSync('cargo', cargoArgs, {encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 20 * 1024 * 1024});
if (r.error) throw r.error;
process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({success: r.status === 0, exit_code: r.status, stdout: r.stdout || '', stderr: r.stderr || ''}));

const fs = require('fs');
const evidence = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8');
if (String(process.env.TEST_SUCCEEDED).toLowerCase() === 'true') {
  throw new Error('The new regression test passed before production remediation; aborting because test-first reproduction was not established.');
}
process.stdout.write(`Regression failed before remediation with exit code ${process.env.TEST_EXIT_CODE}.\n${evidence}`);

